# we cried, He heard, He saw — the separation, our toil — the sons, our oppression — the pressure, He brought us out — not by an angel). Every row READ WHOLE in both
# files (the whole-row rule); the cuts by ch26_ink.SP_. Sitting 17's form.
from ch26_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(301, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL RESPOND AND SAY" (26:5) — RESPONSE IS SAID HERE AND RESPONSE IS SAID THERE (27:14); AS THE RESPONSE THERE IS IN THE HOLY TONGUE, SO THE RESPONSE HERE IS IN THE HOLY TONGUE. The head row of piska 301 ({SP_(301, 1, "נאמר", "כאן", "עניה", "ונאמר", "להלן", "עניה")} "response is said here and response is said there"; {SP_(301, 1, "בלשון", "הקדש")} "in the holy tongue"): THE LANGUAGE PARAMETER of the recital — Hebrew, by the verbal analogy of "respond" with the Levites\' response at Ebal (I2; Sotah 7:2-3 the answer sheet: the first-fruits\' declaration among the things said in the holy tongue); the row cites 27:14 — this sitting\'s own chapter, the dump listed it among chapter 27\'s outside rows. Fresh.')
srow(301, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'HENCE: AT FIRST WHOEVER KNEW HOW TO RECITE RECITED, AND WHOEVER DID NOT, THEY RECITED FOR HIM; PEOPLE REFRAINED FROM BRINGING; THEY ORDAINED THAT THEY RECITE FOR THE KNOWING AND THE UNKNOWING ALIKE, RESTING ON THE VERSE "AND YOU SHALL RESPOND" — RESPONSE IS ONLY FROM ANOTHER\'S MOUTH. ({SP_(301, 2, "בראשונה", "כל", "מי", "שהוא", "יודע", "לקרות", "קורא")} "at first whoever knew how to recite recited"; {SP_(301, 2, "נמנעו", "מלהביא")} "they refrained from bringing"; {SP_(301, 2, "אין", "עניה", "אלא", "מפי", "אחרים")} "response is only from the mouth of others"): THE PROMPTING — the Sages\' ordinance for the illiterate\'s shame (Bikkurim 3:7 inside the spine); the compile\'s ordinance as a parameter on the rite. Fresh.')
srow(301, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SAY BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD: AN ARAMEAN DESTROYING MY FATHER" — THIS TEACHES THAT OUR FATHER JACOB WENT DOWN TO ARAM ONLY TO BE DESTROYED, AND IT IS RECKONED TO LABAN THE ARAMEAN AS IF HE HAD DESTROYED HIM. ({SP_(301, 3, "מלמד", "שלא", "ירד", "אבינו", "יעקב", "לארם")} "teaches that our father Jacob went down to Aram"; {SP_(301, 3, "ומעלה", "על", "לבן", "הארמי", "כאלו", "אבדו")} "and it is reckoned to Laban the Aramean as if he destroyed him"): THE ARAMEAN IS LABAN — "wandering" read as "destroying", the verb transitive; ONKELOS WRITES THE SAME (26:5\'s row: "Laban the Aramean sought to destroy my father"); the Haggadah\'s reading (the translator\'s note at 301:4). Fresh.')
srow(301, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE WENT DOWN TO EGYPT" — NOT TO SETTLE BUT TO SOJOURN; LEST YOU SAY HE WENT DOWN TO TAKE A ROYAL CROWN — "AND SOJOURNED THERE"; WITH A GREAT MULTITUDE? "FEW IN NUMBER", AS IT SAYS "WITH SEVENTY PERSONS YOUR FATHERS WENT DOWN" (10:22). ({SP_(301, 4, "שלא", "ירד", "להשתקע", "אלא", "לגור", "שם")} "not to settle but to sojourn there"; {SP_(301, 4, "יכול", "באוכלוסים", "הרבה")} "could it be with great crowds?"; {SP_(301, 4, "בשבעים", "נפש", "ירדו", "אבותיך", "מצרימה")} "with seventy persons your fathers went down to Egypt"): THE SOJOURN and THE SEVENTY — 10:22\'s count the recital\'s "few" (the tape\'s own seat at Genesis 46). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 10, deu_10_ekev).')
srow(301, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE BECAME THERE A GREAT NATION" — THIS TEACHES THAT ISRAEL WERE DISTINGUISHED THERE. ({SP_(301, 5, "מלמד", "שהיו", "ישראל", "מצינים", "שם")} "teaches that Israel were distinguished there"): the greatness read as distinctness in Egypt. Fresh.')
srow(301, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE SAW OUR AFFLICTION" — AS IT SAYS "AND YOU SHALL LOOK UPON THE BIRTHSTOOLS" (EXODUS 1:16). ({SP_(301, 6, "וראיתן", "על", "האבנים")} "and you shall look upon the birthstools"): the affliction the midwives\' decree — the recital\'s words glossed by the Exodus narrative (the row cites Exodus 1:16 with "there" for the book). Fresh.')
srow(301, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND OUR TOIL" — AS IT SAYS "EVERY SON THAT IS BORN YOU SHALL CAST INTO THE RIVER" (EXODUS 1:22). ({SP_(301, 7, "כל", "הבן", "הילוד", "היארה", "תשליכהו")} "every son born — into the river you shall cast him"): the toil the sons drowned (301:16 repeats it in the Haggadah\'s rows); the translator supplies 26:8\'s text lacking in the Sifrei. Fresh.')
srow(301, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"GREAT AND MIGHTY" — AS IT IS WRITTEN "AND THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL WERE FRUITFUL AND TEEMED AND MULTIPLIED AND GREW EXCEEDINGLY MIGHTY, AND THE LAND WAS FILLED WITH THEM" (EXODUS 1:7). THE FIRST OF THE BRACKETED ROWS 8-24 — the Haggadah\'s recital in the export\'s own unpointed orthography ({SP_(301, 8, "ובני", "ישראל", "פרו", "וישרצו", "וירבו", "ויעצמו")} "and the children of Israel were fruitful and teemed and multiplied and grew mighty"): "poorly attested in copies of Sifre" (the translator at 301:4) — kept whole as the export gives it. Fresh.')
srow(301, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND MANY" — AS IT IS WRITTEN "I MADE YOU A MYRIAD AS THE GROWTH OF THE FIELD, AND YOU INCREASED AND GREW AND CAME TO EXCELLENT BEAUTY" (EZEKIEL 16:7). ({SP_(301, 9, "רבבה", "כצמח", "השדה", "נתתיך")} "a myriad as the growth of the field I made you"): the prophet\'s seat for "many" — the Prophets not read ahead; the citation kept. Fresh.')
srow(301, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE EGYPTIANS DEALT ILL WITH US" (26:6) — AS IT IS WRITTEN "COME, LET US DEAL WISELY WITH THEM LEST THEY MULTIPLY, AND WHEN WAR BEFALLS …" (EXODUS 1:10). ({SP_(301, 10, "הבה", "נתחכמה", "לו", "פן", "ירבה")} "come, let us deal wisely with him lest he multiply"): the ill-dealing Pharaoh\'s counsel. Fresh.')
srow(301, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND AFFLICTED US" — AS IT IS WRITTEN "THEY SET TASKMASTERS OVER THEM TO AFFLICT THEM WITH THEIR BURDENS, AND THEY BUILT STORE-CITIES FOR PHARAOH" (EXODUS 1:11). ({SP_(301, 11, "וישימו", "עליו", "שרי", "מסים", "למען", "ענותו", "בסבלותם")} "they set over him taskmasters to afflict him with their burdens"): the affliction the taskmasters. Fresh.')
srow(301, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND LAID ON US HARD BONDAGE" — AS IT IS WRITTEN "AND EGYPT MADE THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL SERVE WITH RIGOR, AND MADE THEIR LIVES BITTER WITH HARD BONDAGE, IN MORTAR AND IN BRICK AND IN ALL WORK OF THE FIELD" (EXODUS 1:13-14). ({SP_(301, 12, "ויעבידו", "מצרים", "את", "בני", "ישראל", "בפרך")} "and Egypt made the children of Israel serve with rigor"; {SP_(301, 12, "בחומר", "ובלבנים")} "in mortar and in bricks"): the hard bondage Exodus 1:14\'s own words — 26:6\'s one shared token with it. Fresh.')
srow(301, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WE CRIED TO THE LORD, THE GOD OF OUR FATHERS" (26:7) — AS IT IS WRITTEN "IN THOSE MANY DAYS THE KING OF EGYPT DIED, AND THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL SIGHED FROM THE BONDAGE AND CRIED" (EXODUS 2:23). ({SP_(301, 13, "וימת", "מלך", "מצרים")} "and the king of Egypt died"; {SP_(301, 13, "ויאנחו", "בני", "ישראל", "מן", "העבודה", "ויזעקו")} "and the children of Israel sighed from the bondage and cried"): the cry at the king\'s death (Numbers 20:16\'s "we cried" the recital\'s only Torah twin). Fresh.')
srow(301, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE LORD HEARD OUR VOICE" — AS IT IS WRITTEN "AND GOD HEARD THEIR GROANING" (EXODUS 2:24). ({SP_(301, 14, "וישמע", "א-להים", "את", "נאקתם")} "and God heard their groaning"): the hearing Exodus 2:24\'s (Onkelos at 26:7: "received our prayer"). Fresh.')
srow(301, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE SAW OUR AFFLICTION" — THIS IS THE SEPARATION FROM THE WAY OF THE WORLD, AS IT IS WRITTEN "AND GOD SAW THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL AND GOD KNEW" (EXODUS 2:25). ({SP_(301, 15, "זו", "פרישות", "דרך", "ארץ")} "this is the separation from the way of the world"): THE AFFLICTION READ AS THE SEPARATION OF HUSBANDS AND WIVES — the Haggadah\'s reading against 301:6\'s birthstools (two readings of one word in one piska, the bracketed rows the second). Fresh.')
srow(301, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND OUR TOIL" — THESE ARE THE SONS, AS IT IS WRITTEN "EVERY SON BORN YOU SHALL CAST INTO THE RIVER, AND EVERY DAUGHTER YOU SHALL KEEP ALIVE" (EXODUS 1:22). ({SP_(301, 16, "אלו", "הבנים")} "these are the sons"; {SP_(301, 16, "וכל", "הבת", "תחיון")} "and every daughter you shall keep alive"): the toil the sons — 301:7 again with the daughters\' clause. Fresh.')
srow(301, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND OUR OPPRESSION" — THIS IS THE PRESSURE, AS IT IS WRITTEN "AND I HAVE ALSO SEEN THE OPPRESSION WITH WHICH THE EGYPTIANS OPPRESS THEM" (EXODUS 3:9). ({SP_(301, 17, "זו", "הדחק")} "this is the pressure"; {SP_(301, 17, "אשר", "מצרים", "לוחצים", "אותם")} "with which Egypt oppresses them"): the oppression Exodus 3:9\'s word (Onkelos: "our pressure", duchkana). Fresh.')
srow(301, 18, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE LORD BROUGHT US OUT" (26:8) — NOT BY AN ANGEL, NOT BY A SERAPH, NOT BY A MESSENGER, AS IT IS WRITTEN "I WILL PASS THROUGH THE LAND OF EGYPT THIS NIGHT AND SMITE …" (EXODUS 12:12): "I WILL PASS THROUGH" — I AND NOT AN ANGEL; "I WILL SMITE EVERY FIRSTBORN" — I AND NOT A SERAPH; "ON ALL THE GODS OF EGYPT I WILL DO JUDGMENTS" — I AND NOT THE MESSENGER; "I AM THE LORD". ({SP_(301, 18, "אני", "ולא", "מלאך")} "I and not an angel"; {SP_(301, 18, "אני", "ולא", "שרף")} "I and not a seraph"; {SP_(301, 18, "אני", "ולא", "השליח")} "I and not the messenger"): THE AGENT — the exodus\'s own act, Exodus 12:12\'s three clauses read as three denials; the tape\'s night of the plague the seat. Fresh.')
